From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:03:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: tell the firmware which MSI wakes the host

The QMI host capability message has a field for the MSI that the
firmware sends to wake the host from WoW, the one assigned to the WAKE
user. ath11k never filled it in. The QCA6390 firmware then recognises
a magic packet but has no way to signal it, and the host sleeps on.

Send the WAKE MSI data, as the vendor driver does.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
index 7dc07339b9..9943d92f2f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -1711,7 +1711,9 @@ int ath11k_qmi_host_cap_send(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct qmi_wlanfw_host_cap_req_msg_v01 req;
 	struct qmi_wlanfw_host_cap_resp_msg_v01 resp;
+	u32 user_base_data, base_vector;
 	struct qmi_txn txn;
+	int num_vectors;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	memset(&req, 0, sizeof(req));
@@ -1758,6 +1760,17 @@ int ath11k_qmi_host_cap_send(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 
 	req.nm_modem |= PLATFORM_CAP_PCIE_PME_D3COLD;
 
+	/*
+	 * The firmware wakes the host from WoW with an MSI of its own, the
+	 * one assigned to the WAKE user. Without it the firmware sees a
+	 * wake event but has no way to signal it.
+	 */
+	if (!ath11k_get_user_msi_vector(ab, "WAKE", &num_vectors,
+					&user_base_data, &base_vector)) {
+		req.wake_msi_valid = 1;
+		req.wake_msi = user_base_data;
+	}
+
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_QMI, "host cap request\n");
 
 	ret = qmi_txn_init(&ab->qmi.handle, &txn,
